-- The hostile reading: evidence for the findings in NOTES.md section 4.
--
-- Each assertion below states the SURPRISING answer, so it passes while the defect is in the
-- instrument; a finding that only reading can show is in NOTES.md and not here. The figures
-- are scenario inputs (a sum insured of 500,000,000 and so on), not figures from the document.
-- The clauses are quoted in the rule modules; here they are cited by source line.

§ `Findings`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN eff IS A DATE
      dob IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The contract`
`a contract effective` eff `for an insured born` dob MEANS
    `The contract` WITH
        `effective date`                                              IS eff
        `date the Company accepted the insurance`                     IS eff PLUS 10
        `date of the last reinstatement`                              IS NOTHING
        `date of the last increase of the current sum insured`        IS NOTHING
        `insured's date of birth`                                     IS dob
        `premium mode`                                                IS annual
        `annualised basic premium of the first contract year`         IS 12_000_000
        `accepted on standard terms at issue or at the last reinstatement` IS TRUE

`C1` MEANS `a contract effective` (YMD 2021 1 31) `for an insured born` (YMD 1980 6 15)
`C2` MEANS `a contract effective` (YMD 2021 4 15) `for an insured born` (YMD 2021 3 1)

GIVEN opt IS A `A benefit option`
      b   IS A NUMBER
      a   IS A NUMBER
      k   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The state of the contract`
`in force with` opt `, sum insured 500,000,000, basic value` b `, accumulation value` a `, cancer paid` k MEANS
    `The state of the contract` WITH
        `in force`                    IS TRUE
        `benefit option`              IS opt
        `current sum insured`         IS 500_000_000
        `basic account value`         IS b
        `accumulation account value`  IS a
        `outstanding debts`           IS 0
        `cancer benefit already paid` IS k

GIVEN fraud IS A BOOLEAN
      war   IS A BOOLEAN
      since IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The cause of a death or disability`
`a cause, fraud` fraud `, war` war `, existing since` since MEANS
    `The cause of a death or disability` WITH
        `an act of insurance fraud`    IS fraud
        `suicide or attempted suicide` IS FALSE
        `date the cause first existed` IS since
        `war`                          IS war

GIVEN d  IS A DATE
      c  IS A `The cause of a death or disability`
      ns IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A death`
`a death without accident on` d `, cause` c `, non-smoker` ns MEANS
    `A death` WITH
        `date of death`                     IS d
        `the cause`                         IS c
        `the accident`                      IS NOTHING
        `determined to be a non-smoker`     IS ns
        `premiums received after the death` IS 0
        `the beneficiaries`                 IS EMPTY
        `the policyholder has died`         IS FALSE

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `The aggregate limit at the time of payment`
`no limit raised, already received` x MEANS
    `The aggregate limit at the time of payment` WITH
        `limit published at the time of payment`                              IS NOTHING
        `the same kind of benefit already received under all contracts with the Company` IS x

§§ `FD1 — 1.9 and Article 4 give different maturity dates`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 287-288, 546-548, 648-650)
-- Insured born 15 June 1980, contract effective 31 January 2021. Article 4: the anniversary after
-- the 100th birthday, 31 January 2081. 1.9 read with 1.32: insurance age 100 is reached on
-- 31 January 2081, so the anniversary after that, 31 January 2082. One year of cover, and the
-- date the account value is paid out (7.1), turn on which clause governs.
#ASSERT `1.9 — the maturity date of` `C1` EQUALS YMD 2081 1 31
#ASSERT `1.9 read with 1.32 — the maturity date of` `C1` EQUALS YMD 2082 1 31

§§ `FD2 — 1.32 makes the policyholder's 18 years the insured's age`

-- A 16-year-old policyholder insuring a 40-year-old qualifies on the literal reading, and not on
-- the reading taken.
`a 16-year-old policyholder` MEANS
    `A policyholder` WITH
        `an organisation`                     IS FALSE
        `date of birth`                       IS JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)
        `full civil act capacity`             IS TRUE
        `declared and signed the application` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `1.2 read literally with 1.32 — the policyholder` `a 16-year-old policyholder` `qualifies, the insured's insurance age being` 40
#ASSERT NOT `1.2 — the policyholder` `a 16-year-old policyholder` `qualifies on` (YMD 2021 3 1)

§§ `FD3 — the incontestability clause protects nothing the contract would otherwise contest`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 754-757)
-- An intentional misstatement can be contested ten years on; an innocent one can be contested
-- in the first two years, but 6.2 gives no remedy for it.
`an intentional misstatement` MEANS `A misstatement` WITH `intentional` IS TRUE, `with correct information the Company would have` IS `declined to insure the insured`
`an innocent misstatement` MEANS `A misstatement` WITH `intentional` IS FALSE, `with correct information the Company would have` IS `declined to insure the insured`
#ASSERT `6.3 — the information behind` `an intentional misstatement` `under` `C1` `may still be contested on` (YMD 2031 2 1) `, in force with the insured alive at the end of the two years:` TRUE
#ASSERT `6.3 — the information behind` `an innocent misstatement` `under` `C1` `may still be contested on` (YMD 2022 2 1) `, in force with the insured alive at the end of the two years:` TRUE
#ASSERT `6.2 — the remedies open to the Company for` `an innocent misstatement` EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `FD4 — the pre-existing-cause exclusion has no time limit`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1141, 1145, 1151, 1157)
-- A death in 2060 from a condition that existed on 1 January 2021, a month before the effective
-- date: the basic benefit pays the account value of 50,000,000 instead of 550,000,000.
`S` MEANS `in force with` `the basic benefit` `, sum insured 500,000,000, basic value` 40_000_000 `, accumulation value` 10_000_000 `, cancer paid` 0
#ASSERT `the benefit on the death under` `C1` `, at` `S` `, on` (`a death without accident on` (YMD 2060 6 1) `, cause` (`a cause, fraud` FALSE `, war` FALSE `, existing since` (YMD 2021 1 1)) `, non-smoker` TRUE) `, limit` (`no limit raised, already received` 0) EQUALS 50000000
#ASSERT `the benefit on the death under` `C1` `, at` `S` `, on` (`a death without accident on` (YMD 2060 6 1) `, cause` (`a cause, fraud` FALSE `, war` FALSE `, existing since` (YMD 2021 2 1)) `, non-smoker` TRUE) `, limit` (`no limit raised, already received` 0) EQUALS 550000000

§§ `FD5 — an excluded death can pay more than a covered one`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1017-1018, 1151, 1157)
-- The basic benefit, an account value of 600,000,000 above the sum insured of 500,000,000, a
-- cancer benefit of 125,000,000 paid earlier, a smoker. A covered death pays the greater of
-- 500,000,000 and 600,000,000 less 125,000,000 = 475,000,000; a death in war, excluded by 8.1,
-- pays the account value of 600,000,000 with nothing deducted, because 7.5 deducts only from a
-- 7.2 or 7.3 benefit.
`S rich after cancer` MEANS `in force with` `the basic benefit` `, sum insured 500,000,000, basic value` 500_000_000 `, accumulation value` 100_000_000 `, cancer paid` 125_000_000
#ASSERT `the benefit on the death under` `C1` `, at` `S rich after cancer` `, on` (`a death without accident on` (YMD 2040 6 1) `, cause` (`a cause, fraud` FALSE `, war` FALSE `, existing since` (YMD 2040 1 1)) `, non-smoker` FALSE) `, limit` (`no limit raised, already received` 0) EQUALS 475000000
#ASSERT `the benefit on the death under` `C1` `, at` `S rich after cancer` `, on` (`a death without accident on` (YMD 2040 6 1) `, cause` (`a cause, fraud` FALSE `, war` TRUE `, existing since` (YMD 2040 1 1)) `, non-smoker` FALSE) `, limit` (`no limit raised, already received` 0) EQUALS 600000000

§§ `FD6 — the accidental-death limit, read as written, is a cliff`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 969, 977, 984-985)
-- 9,800,000,000 already received under other contracts: read as a cap, 200,000,000 of the
-- 500,000,000 is paid; read as the condition it is written as, nothing.
#ASSERT `7.4 and 7.5 — the benefit of` 500000000 `kept within the limit, under` (`no limit raised, already received` 9800000000) EQUALS 200000000
#ASSERT `7.4 read as a condition — the benefit of` 500000000 `under` (`no limit raised, already received` 9800000000) EQUALS 0

§§ `FD7 — a cancer claim can be out of time before the cancer is diagnosed`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 472-474, 2280-2281)
-- Symptoms on 1 March 2023 that would send an ordinary person to a doctor; diagnosis 1 May
-- 2024; claim on 2 May 2024. The cancer "arose" on 1 March 2023, and the twelve months ended on
-- 1 March 2024, before the diagnosis.
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of claim`
      ev IS A DATE
      made IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A claim`
`a claim of kind` k `for an event on` ev `, made on` made MEANS
    `A claim` WITH
        `kind`                                                 IS k
        `caused by an accident`                                IS FALSE
        `date of the insured event`                            IS ev
        `date the claim was made`                              IS made
        `days spent supplying documents under 27.3 and 27.4`   IS 0
        `the documents`                                        IS `The documents submitted` WITH
                                                                   `claim form completed fully and accurately` IS TRUE
                                                                   `extract of the death record` IS FALSE
                                                                   `certificate of the injury rate from the medical assessment council or an approved foreign medical organisation` IS TRUE
                                                                   `medical evidence from the examining, diagnosing or treating doctor` IS TRUE
                                                                   `accident record, scene examination record, forensic and investigation conclusions certified by the competent authority` IS FALSE
                                                                   `proof of the right to the benefit, such as a will, and identity papers of the person entitled` IS TRUE
                                                                   `proof of the right to receive the benefit, such as an authorisation` IS TRUE
        `date the complete and valid file was received`        IS NOTHING
#ASSERT `28 — the last day to claim` (`a claim of kind` `a cancer claim` `for an event on` (YMD 2023 3 1) `, made on` (YMD 2024 5 2)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2024 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `28 — the claim is made in time` (`a claim of kind` `a cancer claim` `for an event on` (YMD 2023 3 1) `, made on` (YMD 2024 5 2))

§§ `FD8 — the disability certificate and the claim deadline squeeze each other`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 462-463)
-- A disability on 1 March 2023 can be certified under 1.29(b) no earlier than 1 September 2023,
-- and the claim must be made by 1 March 2024. A certificate issued on 2 March 2024, after a
-- slow council, satisfies 1.29(b), but the claim it supports is out of time.
`a disability certified on 2 March 2024` MEANS
    `A disability` WITH
        `date of the disability`                         IS YMD 2023 3 1
        `hands lost or irrecoverably paralysed`          IS 0
        `legs lost or irrecoverably paralysed`           IS 0
        `eyes totally and permanently blind`             IS 0
        `certified rate of disability or of permanent loss of working capacity` IS JUST 0.85
        `certified by`                                   IS `a provincial or centrally-run city medical assessment council`
        `date of the certification`                      IS JUST (YMD 2024 3 2)
        `the cause`                                      IS `a cause, fraud` FALSE `, war` FALSE `, existing since` (YMD 2023 3 1)
#ASSERT `1.29 — the disability is total and permanent` `a disability certified on 2 March 2024`
#ASSERT NOT `28 — the claim is made in time` (`a claim of kind` `a disability claim` `for an event on` (YMD 2023 3 1) `, made on` (YMD 2024 3 2))

§§ `FD9 — temporary insurance: a larger first premium can yield less`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 655-658, 665-667)
-- First premiums of 99,000,000 on an accidental death: the benefit of 100,000,000. First
-- premiums of 100,500,000: no benefit, and a refund of 100,500,000 less 2,000,000 of medical
-- costs, 98,500,000.
GIVEN prem IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A death during temporary insurance`
`an accidental death in temporary cover, first premiums` prem MEANS
    `A death during temporary insurance` WITH
        `date the application was completed and the first premium paid in full` IS YMD 2021 3 1
        `date the temporary cover ended`                                       IS NOTHING
        `date of death`                                                        IS YMD 2021 3 10
        `the accident`                                                         IS JUST (`An accident` WITH `date of the accident` IS YMD 2021 3 9, `by the impact of a sudden, external force or object` IS TRUE, `unintended and against the will of the insured` IS TRUE, `the direct and sole cause, unrelated to any other cause` IS TRUE, `excluded circumstances` IS EMPTY)
        `suicide`                                                              IS FALSE
        `total sum insured of all applications for the same insured`           IS 1_000_000_000
        `total first premiums paid on all applications for the same insured`   IS prem
        `medical examination costs`                                            IS 2_000_000
#ASSERT `5.1 — the temporary insurance benefit` (`an accidental death in temporary cover, first premiums` 99000000) EQUALS 100000000
#ASSERT `5.1 — the temporary insurance benefit` (`an accidental death in temporary cover, first premiums` 100500000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Article 5 — the first premiums refunded` (`an accidental death in temporary cover, first premiums` 100500000) EQUALS 98500000

§§ `FD10 — the withdrawal cap locks in the accumulation account`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1255, 1257-1259)
-- 300,000,000 in the accumulation account, 10,000,000 in the basic account: no more than
-- 8,000,000 may be withdrawn, though 9.2 takes it from the accumulation account.
`S lopsided` MEANS `in force with` `the basic benefit` `, sum insured 500,000,000, basic value` 10_000_000 `, accumulation value` 300_000_000 `, cancer paid` 0
GIVEN amt IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A withdrawal request`
`a withdrawal in 2025 of` amt MEANS
    `A withdrawal request` WITH
        `date of the request`                     IS YMD 2025 3 1
        `amount requested`                        IS amt
        `minimum set by the Company at the time`  IS 1_000_000
#ASSERT `9.1 — the policyholder may request the withdrawal under` `C1` `, at` `S lopsided` `:` (`a withdrawal in 2025 of` 8000000)
#ASSERT NOT `9.1 — the policyholder may request the withdrawal under` `C1` `, at` `S lopsided` `:` (`a withdrawal in 2025 of` 8000001)

§§ `FD11 — a withdrawal reduces the sum insured by an amount 9.3 does not state`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1265-1267)
-- The same withdrawal of 8,000,000, taken wholly from the accumulation account, leaves the basic
-- account at 10,000,000, below the sum insured, so 9.3 fires; by how much it reduces the sum
-- insured, the clause does not say.
#ASSERT `9.3 — the current sum insured is to be reduced, at` `S lopsided` `:` (`a withdrawal in 2025 of` 8000000)
#ASSERT REFUSED `9.3 — the current sum insured after the withdrawal, at` `S lopsided` `:` (`a withdrawal in 2025 of` 8000000)

§§ `FD12 — read literally, Article 16 deducts the monthly deduction twice`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1733, 1754-1755)
-- 100,000 in the basic account, 2,000,000 in the accumulation account, a deduction of 180,000.
-- Read literally: the basic account goes to -80,000 and the accumulation account loses the whole
-- 180,000 too, 360,000 in all.
`a short month` MEANS
    `A month on the account` WITH
        `basic account value at the previous monthiversary`                 IS 100_000
        `accumulation account value at the previous monthiversary`          IS 2_000_000
        `basic premiums paid since the previous monthiversary`              IS 0
        `premium year of the basic premiums paid`                           IS 6
        `accumulation premiums paid since the previous monthiversary`       IS 0
        `interest on the basic account value at the previous month's rate`  IS 0
        `interest on the accumulation account value at the previous month's rate` IS 0
        `cost of insurance for the month`                                   IS 150_000
        `contract administration charge for the month`                      IS 30_000
        `withdrawals from the basic account value since the previous monthiversary` IS 0
        `withdrawals from the accumulation account value since the previous monthiversary` IS 0
#ASSERT `16, read literally — the account at the monthiversary` `a short month` EQUALS `The account at a monthiversary` WITH `basic account value` IS (0 MINUS 80000), `accumulation account value` IS 1820000, `monthly deduction left unpaid` IS 0
#ASSERT `16 — the account at the monthiversary` `a short month` EQUALS `The account at a monthiversary` WITH `basic account value` IS 0, `accumulation account value` IS 1920000, `monthly deduction left unpaid` IS 0

§§ `FD13 — the free-look period depends on whether delivery counts`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1888-1889)
-- Issued 1 March 2023, received 15 March 2023, refused 30 March 2023: in time counting from
-- receipt (to 5 April), out of time counting from issue (to 22 March).
`a late-delivered contract refused on 30 March 2023` MEANS
    `A free-look refusal` WITH
        `date the contract was issued`                IS YMD 2023 3 1
        `date the policyholder received the contract` IS YMD 2023 3 15
        `date of the refusal`                         IS YMD 2023 3 30
        `premiums paid`                               IS 20_000_000
        `medical examination costs`                   IS 0
#ASSERT `21 — the refusal is in time` `a late-delivered contract refused on 30 March 2023`
#ASSERT NOT `21, counted from issue — the refusal is in time` `a late-delivered contract refused on 30 March 2023`

§§ `FD14 — the last row of the loyalty-bonus table says 6 in figures and five in words`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1111-1113)
-- With interest of k x 100,000 in contract year k, the numeral (year 6) gives a base of 50% of
-- 4,000,000 = 2,000,000 on the 10th anniversary; the word (year 5) gives 50% of 4,500,000 =
-- 2,250,000, and a 10th-anniversary bonus of 7,750,000 instead of 7,500,000.
`R` MEANS
    `The record for the loyalty bonus` WITH
        `interest credited to the basic account value, by contract year` IS LIST 100000, 200000, 300000, 400000, 500000, 600000, 700000, 800000, 900000, 1000000
        `basic premiums of earlier contract years paid in full at each due date, grace period included` IS TRUE
        `the two most recent monthly basic premiums paid in full before the bonus date` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `7.7 — the bonus base recorded under` `R` `on anniversary` 10 EQUALS 2000000
#ASSERT 50% TIMES (`the interest credited under` `R` `from contract year` 5 `to contract year` 10) EQUALS 2250000
#ASSERT `7.7 — the loyalty bonus under` `C1` `and` `R` `on anniversary` 10 EQUALS 7500000

§§ `FD15 — one beneficiary's fraud costs the others the death benefit`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 565-567, 1137, 1185-1188)
-- A beneficiary who kills the insured to collect commits "hành vi gian lận bảo hiểm" (1.33).
-- 8.1 then excludes the 7.2 and 7.3 benefits for every beneficiary, leaving the account value of
-- 50,000,000 against 550,000,000; 8.2 keeps the innocent beneficiaries' shares of 7.4, 8.1
-- has no such saving. LAW: Article 40(2) of the Law on Insurance Business (aid, line 830)
-- requires payment to the other beneficiaries.
#ASSERT `the benefit on the death under` `C1` `, at` `S` `, on` (`a death without accident on` (YMD 2040 6 1) `, cause` (`a cause, fraud` TRUE `, war` FALSE `, existing since` (YMD 2040 6 1)) `, non-smoker` TRUE) `, limit` (`no limit raised, already received` 0) EQUALS 50000000

§§ `FD21 — a cancer benefit can exceed the child's reduced death benefit`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 926-927, 940, 993, 1017-1018)
-- C2's insured, born 1 March 2021: a cancer arising on 1 August 2021, after the 90 days from
-- acceptance on 25 April 2021, pays 25% of 500,000,000 = 125,000,000. A death on 1 March 2022,
-- still insurance age 0, pays 20% of 500,000,000 = 100,000,000 under 7.2, less than the
-- 125,000,000 to be deducted from it. The document does not say what follows.
`S child` MEANS `in force with` `the basic benefit` `, sum insured 500,000,000, basic value` 10_000_000 `, accumulation value` 0 `, cancer paid` 0
`S child after cancer` MEANS `in force with` `the basic benefit` `, sum insured 500,000,000, basic value` 10_000_000 `, accumulation value` 0 `, cancer paid` 125_000_000
`a cancer on 1 August 2021` MEANS
    `A cancer` WITH
        `a malignant tumour confirmed by histology, growing uncontrollably and invading tissue` IS TRUE
        `date the cancer arose`                                        IS YMD 2021 8 1
        `pre-malignant, non-invasive or in situ, or of borderline or low malignancy` IS FALSE
        `a tumour of the prostate, thyroid or bladder classified T1N0M0` IS FALSE
        `chronic lymphocytic leukaemia`                                IS FALSE
        `RAI stage`                                                    IS NOTHING
        `in the presence of HIV infection`                            IS FALSE
        `a skin cancer`                                                IS FALSE
        `malignant melanoma`                                           IS FALSE
        `Breslow depth in millimetres`                                 IS NOTHING
        `Clark level`                                                  IS NOTHING
#ASSERT `7.5 — the cancer benefit under` `C2` `, at` `S child` `, for` `a cancer on 1 August 2021` `, limit` (`no limit raised, already received` 0) EQUALS 125000000
#ASSERT `7.2.1 — the death or disability benefit, at` `S child after cancer` `, at insurance age` 0 EQUALS 100000000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the benefit on the death under` `C2` `, at` `S child after cancer` `, on` (`a death without accident on` (YMD 2022 3 1) `, cause` (`a cause, fraud` FALSE `, war` FALSE `, existing since` (YMD 2022 2 1)) `, non-smoker` TRUE) `, limit` (`no limit raised, already received` 0)

§§ `FD27 — the loyalty-bonus windows overlap`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1076, 1082-1083)
-- Interest of 1,000,000 credited in contract year 6 and nothing in any other year: year 6 lies
-- in all five windows, so the total base is 5 x 50% x 1,000,000 = 2,500,000, and the 10th-
-- anniversary bonus pays two and a half times that year's interest.
`R year 6 only` MEANS
    `The record for the loyalty bonus` WITH
        `interest credited to the basic account value, by contract year` IS LIST 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1000000, 0, 0, 0, 0
        `basic premiums of earlier contract years paid in full at each due date, grace period included` IS TRUE
        `the two most recent monthly basic premiums paid in full before the bonus date` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `7.7 — the loyalty bonus under` `C1` `and` `R year 6 only` `on anniversary` 10 EQUALS 2500000

§§ `FD28 — 27.1 asks for a certificate that 1.29(b) does not accept`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 460-462, 2215, 2221-2222)
-- 27.1 lists a certificate from "tổ chức y tế hợp pháp ở nước ngoài được chúng tôi chấp thuận";
-- 1.29(b) accepts only a provincial council or an independent medical organisation approved by
-- the Company. A 90% certificate from an approved foreign organisation is not a 1.29(b)
-- disability.
`a disability certified abroad` MEANS
    `A disability` WITH
        `date of the disability`                         IS YMD 2023 3 1
        `hands lost or irrecoverably paralysed`          IS 0
        `legs lost or irrecoverably paralysed`           IS 0
        `eyes totally and permanently blind`             IS 0
        `certified rate of disability or of permanent loss of working capacity` IS JUST 0.9
        `certified by`                                   IS `a lawful foreign medical organisation approved by the Company`
        `date of the certification`                      IS JUST (YMD 2023 10 1)
        `the cause`                                      IS `a cause, fraud` FALSE `, war` FALSE `, existing since` (YMD 2023 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `1.29 — the disability is total and permanent` `a disability certified abroad`

§§ `Article 29 left unperformed`

-- If the Company neither settles within 30 days nor settles with interest afterwards, the
-- reparation has no deadline in the document; the trace shows what is left standing.
#TRACE `29 — the Company's duty to settle` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
